pped sleeping. I am the one who drives my little sister everywhere now. This reunion was the first weekend I got to just be a cousin again instead of the responsible one." CR-105,Rosa,Delgado,married,prefers email,,none,,2,,Last summer abuela taught me to make tamales from scratch and this weekend we did it again for the whole crowd. I learned that patience is its own ingredient. Watching everyone go quiet at the first bite was worth every hour on the corn husks. CR-106,Kevin,Chen,married,prefers text,PCR-2026-2003,none,,27,New ADHD diagnosis over the summer; medication adjustment in progress.,"I got diagnosed with ADHD over the summer and the meds still make me feel a little strange some days. The lake was easier though — my head goes quiet near water. Skipping stones with the kids was the calmest I have felt in months." CR-107,Amina,Farouk,married,prefers voice notes,,none,,10,,My favorite moment was the poetry someone read around the fire. It felt like the way I actually think — short and sideways. I want to write something for next year's reunion, maybe in Somali, but I don't have all the words for these feelings yet. CR-108,Nora,Lindqvist,married,"prefers text, hard of hearing",PCR-2026-2004,monitor,A cousin's teasing at the group photo got under her skin; kept an eye on it the rest of the weekend.,19,Was the target of a cousin's teasing; her therapist Dr. Kaur suggested journaling to work through it.,I started a journal this fall because Dr. Kaur said it might help. At first it was just dates and sad faces. By the reunion I was writing whole paragraphs, and one of them was about how the lake at sunrise made me feel brand new. CR-109,Ben,Tanaka,married,prefers email,,none,,8,,My son and I are reading The Hobbit out loud together — one chapter every Sunday since the reunion campfire story night. He does all the dwarf voices and I do Bilbo. It takes us almost an hour because we keep laughing and starting over. CR-110,Tasha,Brooks,newly single,prefers phone calls,,none,,20,,"I used to dread reunions because my life feels messy right now. But everyone just made room for me. The morning I helped grandma flip pancakes and nobody asked a single hard question — that was the kindest thing anyone did all weekend." CR-111,Derek,Foster,married,prefers text,,monitor,Argument during the drive up about who was hosting what; we do weekly check-in calls now and things are steadier.,34,,"I am working on being less short with people. Coach Miller from my running club said anger is just energy with nowhere to go, so I ran the lake trail every morning at the reunion. It helped. Sorry again for snapping in the car." CR-112,Leilani,Wong,married,prefers voice notes,PCR-2026-2005,none,,9,Mother's cancer treatment ongoing; she is the primary caregiver. Extreme sensitivity around any health disclosures.,after my mom's mastectomy I helped with her drains and that was my whole autumn. Bringing her to the lake this weekend, seeing her laugh with her sisters, felt like a reward for all of it. She is okay now. I would write a whole book about her. CR-113,Rachel,Goldman,married,prefers email,PCR-2026-2011,none,,6,,My speech therapist Ms. Levin has been teaching me to slow down so my words come out the way I mean them. At the reunion talent night I actually read a poem out loud in front of everyone. I am getting better and I am proud. CR-114,Sean,O'Brien,married,"prefers text, mornings are hard",PCR-2026-2006,monitor,Showed up late to two group activities; it read as flaky to some cousins but it is really a family logistics thing.,28,Housing instability risk; mornings revolve around his autistic brother's routine. Lateness is family circumstance, not indifference.,"I know I missed the sunrise hike. Mornings are hard at my house because my little brother has autism and getting him out the door takes everything we have. I am not making excuses, just explaining. The afternoon by the lake made up for it." CR-115,Tyler,Bennett,newly single,prefers text,PCR-2026-2007,estranged,Long-standing rift; barely spoke this weekend and left early after a tense exchange.,36,Vape/substance incident last fall; family started therapy. He is ashamed.,This reunion was hard for me. I made some choices last year I am not proud of. I have been talking to my mom more and we go to family therapy on Wednesdays now. Writing this down in the memory book is part of trying to do better. CR-116,Linh,Nguyen,married,prefers voice notes,,none,,7,,I read on the dock every afternoon and finished three books over the long weekend. My favorite was A Wrinkle in Time. I am writing my own story about a girl who can hear what plants are thinking. It is going to be 200 pages. CR-117,Anjali,Mehta,married,prefers phone calls,,none,,25,,My little cousin and I built a reading fort out of blankets and flashlights in the loft. We read Charlotte's Web together and I cried at the end even though I am supposed to be the grown-up. Caring about the story is a kind of bravery. CR-118,Marcus,Reyes,married,prefers text,,none,,12,,The lake was the only place all weekend where my brain went quiet. We swam out to the raft every afternoon and just floated. I keep telling people the reunion was relaxing and this is exactly what I mean. CR-119,Sofia,Navarro,newly single,"prefers text, replies late",PCR-2026-2008,none,,16,Recently relocated and still settling; going through a lot.,"Everything in my life still feels temporary right now — new town, new routine, new everything. But sitting around the fire with all of you, I felt like I belonged to something steady for the first time in months." CR-120,Grandma,Chen,recently widowed,prefers phone calls,,none,,1,,Having all of my grandchildren in one kitchen again was the answer to a prayer. We rolled tamales, we burned the first batch of pancakes, and nobody minded. This is what I hoped for when I first dreamed up this reunion. CR-121,Uma,Desai,married,prefers email,,none,,4,,Cooking with the family this weekend reminded me that recipes are just instructions you can argue with. Grandma and I disagreed about the salt three times and both of us were right. I love that about this family. CR-122,Victor,Chen,married,prefers text,,none,,26,,People talk fast around the reunion table and I catch every third word. But out on the quiet dock at dusk, one conversation at a time, I could finally keep up. Those slow talks were my favorite part. CR-123,Willa,Cross,married,prefers voice notes,,none,,5,,Our old dog Scout got sick in January and we almost lost her, so I nearly didn't come. Instead I brought her, and watching her nap in the sun by the lake with the kids petting her was healing for both of us. CR-124,Xavier,Chen,married,prefers text,,none,,32,,I filmed little clips of the whole weekend — the campfire, the cannonball contest, grandma laughing. I am cutting them into a short movie for everyone. Turns out capturing a reunion is harder than it looks, but I loved trying. CR-125,Yara,Aziz,married,prefers phone calls,,none,,15,,The reunion fell right at the end of Ramadan this year, so I broke my last few fasts with all of you at the lake. Explaining it to the little cousins over dinner, instead of just quietly fasting alone, made it feel like a celebration. CR-126,Zach,Morrison,married,prefers text,,none,,22,,The quiet cabin porch was where I retreated when the crowd got to be too much. I used to think needing a break meant I was antisocial. This weekend I learned that stepping away and coming back is its own kind of belonging. CR-127,Amira,Khalil,married,"prefers text, replies late",PCR-2026-2009,none,,11,Parents under financial stress; she has been translating bills at home. Watch for stress.,"Money is tight at home and I carry more of it than a kid should. For one weekend at the lake, none of that followed me. I laughed so hard during the three-legged race that I forgot to worry, and I needed that more than anyone knew." CR-128,Brandon,Lee,married,prefers email,,none,,35,,I tend to keep to myself at big gatherings because jumping in feels risky. This reunion, my cousin just handed me a fishing rod and sat with me in silence for an hour. That mattered more than any speech. CR-129,Chloe,Park,married,prefers voice notes,,none,,3,,I brought two rescue dogs from the shelter where I volunteer and they were the stars of the reunion. Watching the whole family fall in love with a scruffy pit bull named Rusty made my year. Animals do not care about anything but kindness. CR-130,Dante,Romano,married,"prefers text, needs quiet",,none,,24,,Big loud group meals are the hardest part for me, so I ate breakfast early on the quiet porch most mornings. Grandma always joined me. Those calm sunrise breakfasts with her were the reunion I will actually remember. CR-131,Elena,Vasquez,married,prefers phone calls,,none,,18,,My grandma tells stories about crossing the border that I am only old enough now to understand. Hearing her tell them again by the fire, with the little ones listening, I finally saw how much of this family she carried here herself. CR-132,Finn,Murphy,newly single,prefers text,PCR-2026-2010,none,,30,Family went through housing instability last fall and doubled up with relatives. He only recently opened up about it; handle gently.,"Last fall was rough and I almost skipped the reunion out of pride. I am so glad I didn't. Nobody asked why my life looked different this year — they just made space for me at the lake and that was everything." CR-133,Gia,Washington,married,prefers email,,none,,14,,Big group toasts make my chest tight, so instead of standing up to speak I wrote everyone a little note and left them on the pillows. Sharing my thanks that way, on my own terms, felt like real growth for me. CR-134,Holden,Price,married,prefers text,,none,,29,,I thought a whole weekend of family togetherness would drive me crazy until my grandfather showed me the little workshop at the cabin. We fixed the dock railing together without a single nail. Patience runs in this family and I am glad I got some of it. CR-135,Isla,Fernandez,married,prefers voice notes,,none,,5,,I learned three ukulele chords over the winter and finally worked up the nerve to play at the campfire. It was shaky, but the little cousins sang along anyway. Music is easier to share than feelings, and this family sang loudest of all. CR-136,Jasper,Cole,married,prefers text,,none,,21,,I am not much of a writer, so leaving something in this memory book is hard for me. But I dictated most of it walking the lake trail and then cleaned it up. It probably still has mistakes. I care more that it sounds honest, like this whole weekend did.
